## 4. MANAGEMENT EVALUATION

### 4.1 The Critical Question

> *"Do they love the money or do they love the business?"*

This is the most vital question. They need founders who:
- Treat the business like a **family heirloom**
- Jump out of bed excited to work
- **Are not** just looking to cash out

### 4.2 Management Traits They Seek

| Trait | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| **Passion for the business itself** | Love the work, not just the wealth |
| **Extreme candor** | Report bad news immediately; treat shareholders as partners |
| **Capital allocation skill** | Retain earnings only if $1 retained creates >$1 of market value |
| **Integrity** | Need to trust completely — "no one had either the ability or integrity" like Tom Murphy |
| **Resistance to institutional imperative** | Think independently, don't copy competitors |

### 4.3 The "Scuttlebutt" Question

The specific question Buffett uses to assess management and industry dynamics:

> *"If you had to go away for 10 years on a desert island and you had to put all of your family's money into one of your competitors, which one would it be and why?"*

Then follow-up: *"If you had a silver bullet to put through the head of one competitor, which one would it be?"*

### 4.4 Tom Murphy — The Gold Standard

Buffett on Capital Cities' Tom Murphy: "No one had either the ability or integrity in terms of the way he ran Cap Cities for decades... he only built it when it made sense, not when it did something for his ego."

